		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=343#comment-15982</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I was a friend of Ayesha&#039;s years ago and knew her through the folk song society and various musical events. She was always kind and full of light. I moved to Arizona in July of 06 and did not know of her passing however I had heard that she was very sick. Now, in 2013, her old friend Terry O&#039;conner and I attended a meditation session in Ardmore. The teacher said &quot; You two have a mutual friend, a healer , she is interested in your conversation about drums, she is glad to be here watching you two. We didn&#039;t know who he was referring to. Then he said
&quot;Her name is Ayesha&quot; well, Jeannie is still around in spirit!!!]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I was a friend of Ayesha&#8217;s years ago and knew her through the folk song society and various musical events. She was always kind and full of light. I moved to Arizona in July of 06 and did not know of her passing however I had heard that she was very sick. Now, in 2013, her old friend Terry O&#8217;conner and I attended a meditation session in Ardmore. The teacher said &#8221; You two have a mutual friend, a healer , she is interested in your conversation about drums, she is glad to be here watching you two. We didn&#8217;t know who he was referring to. Then he said<br />
&#8220;Her name is Ayesha&#8221; well, Jeannie is still around in spirit!!!</p>
]]></content:encoded>
